  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Successful Aimak 2 Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  USAID&apos;s Successful Aimak 2 Activity will continue to promote more effective and inclusive political systems and governing institutions at the local level to strengthen the Kyrgyz Republic&apos;s constituency for democracy. In particular, the activity will focus on: 1) effective service delivery by assisting local governments in improving their ability to effectively manage and finance the delivery of key services, such as solid waste removal and clean water, by using local solutions and public-private partnerships; 2) citizen participation by engaging all citizen groups including women, youth and minorities in the decision making process at the local level. Citizens will also provide feedback on services and advocate for more transparent and accountable governance systems while also seeking avenues for citizen and community organization collaboration with local governments; and 3) local ownership by strengthening the capacity of local stakeholders, such as the Union of Local Self-Governments, to increasingly lead in identifying and addressing development challenges. Fifty municipalities in four provinces will receive technical support to implement more effective services to their communities. This technical support may include training on procurement, legal advice, and increased skill development in budgeting and management. This activity will support ICS objective 3.2: Government institutions that can effectively formulate and implement policies, and provide quality services in an equitable, transparent, and accountable way.  USAID&apos;s contribution to meeting the $12,000,000 DRG directive through this IM is $ 1,200,000.</narrative>
  </description>
